+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time zone,
+  `qty` a whole number of dishes) and answers
+  `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: the tickets imported and the dishes sold
+  on them. Tickets imported before are skipped and not counted. One invalid
+  row (`bad_request`) or one item running out (`sale_out_of_stock`) and
+  nothing is imported; the message names the row (`row 2` is the first data
+  row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }` per item used in
+  those days (inclusive, UTC): `theoretical` is what the sales sold in those
+  days needed, `actual` every `consume` movement, `difference` is
+  `actual - theoretical`.
